{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.QOper","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.satisfiesEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.satisfiesEq","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L107-L114","doc":"**The q-oper equation.** A q-oper A determines the second-order\nq-difference equation on a function y : K → K:\n`y(q²x) − t(x) · y(qx) + Δ(x) · y(x) = 0`.\nThis is the q-analogue of the differential equation on P¹ that the\noper connection encodes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.det_eq_wronskian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.det_eq_wronskian","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L97-L105","doc":"**The determinant of a q-oper is minus the quantum Wronskian.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.quantumWronskian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.quantumWronskian","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L94-L95","doc":"The quantum Wronskian (negative of the (1,2) entry). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.trace","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L91-L92","doc":"The trace function of a q-oper. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.oper_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.oper_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The oper gauge: a₂₂ = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.oper_gauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.oper_gauge","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The oper gauge: a₂₁ = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.toQConnection2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2.toQConnection2","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L85-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QOper2","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L78-L89","doc":"A rank-2 q-connection is a **q-oper** when its (2,1) entry is identically 1\n(the oper gauge). In this gauge, A takes the form:\n```\nA(x) = [ t(x)   -Δ(x) ]\n       [  1      0     ]\n```\nwhere t is the trace and Δ is the quantum Wronskian (determinant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.NonDegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.NonDegenerate","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L72-L74","doc":"A rank-2 q-connection is **non-degenerate** at x if its determinant is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.det","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L68-L70","doc":"The determinant of a rank-2 q-connection at a point x. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₂₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₂₂","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₂₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₂₁","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₁₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₁₂","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₁₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.a₁₁","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The connection matrix entries as functions of x. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.QConnection2","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L59-L66","doc":"A **rank-2 q-connection** is a 2×2 matrix A(x) ∈ GL₂(K(x)) encoding the\nq-difference system σ_q Y = A(x) Y. For a q-oper, A has specific structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_one","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L52-L55","doc":"σ_1 = id. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_compose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_compose","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L47-L50","doc":"q-shift is multiplicative in q: σ_{q₁} ∘ σ_{q₂} = σ_{q₁q₂}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_const","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L42-L45","doc":"The q-shift of a constant is constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift_add","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L37-L40","doc":"The q-shift is linear in the function argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QOper.qShift","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QOper.lean#L34-L35","doc":"The q-shift operator on functions `K → K`: `(σ_q f)(x) = f(q · x)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}